# OQ-3 and PL-18 (L §5.19). "An observed row is in the kind its `kind:` names and in that kind's parents; `o in K`
# tests it" (L §5.19), so r3, of kind groceries under spending under transfers, is in all three (a). Bindings
# (L §5.19): "A binding over an observed input, `o in X over s`, ranges over X's rows dated in s, each once, whether
# or not a version states two of them `same`, since an input's keys are its rows. A binding over an event kind ranges
# over movements ... a pair of rows stated `same` is one movement": over bank_rows three rows, over spending two
# movements, the same pair once (400.00 + 50.00 PLN).
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source bank "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind spending: transfers
kind groceries: spending
input bank_rows: observed
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
version stmt
  cite bank
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-03-02
  bank_rows[r1] = (on: 2026-02-20, kind: groceries, leg cash from konto to world amount 400.00 PLN) "line 1"
  bank_rows[r2] = (on: 2026-02-20, kind: groceries, leg cash from konto to world amount 400.00 PLN) "line 2"
  bank_rows[r3] = (on: 2026-02-21, kind: groceries, leg cash from konto to world amount 50.00 PLN) "line 3"
  same bank_rows[r2] = bank_rows[r1]
ask a: bank_rows[r3] in spending, bank_rows[r3] in groceries, (bank_rows[r3] in transfers)
ask b: count(true for o in bank_rows over 2026-02), count(true for t in spending over 2026-02), sum(t.cash.amount for t in spending over 2026-02)
=== expect
a: (true, true, true)
  cut 2026-10-20
b: (3, 2, 450.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-10-20
